# 🚀 New Domain & Server Installation Guide

This guide details the procedure for deploying this Digital Banking application to a new domain name, establishing Git integration, configuring environment profiles, and initializing database tables and notification templates.

---

## 📅 1. Domain & Web Server Setup (Hostinger)

When migrating your website to a new domain name, configure the pointing and server parameters correctly:

1. **Add Domain to Hostinger**: Log in to your Hostinger hPanel dashboard and navigate to **Websites** -> **Create or Migrate a Website** to add your new domain.
2. **Point Document Root**: Ensure your new domain's Document Root points to the `public/` subdirectory of the repository (e.g., `/public_html/public/`), and **not** the main root directory of the repository. This is critical for security and routing.
3. **Generate SSL Certificate**: Go to the **SSL** settings of your domain inside hPanel, run the automatic installation, and force HTTPS traffic redirect.

---

## 📂 2. Git Setup & Deployment

You can choose to deploy your code from the existing repository or create a brand new one.

### Option A: Reuse the Existing GitHub Repository (Recommended)
You can continue using the existing repository: `https://github.com/ffcu-FrontField/FrontField.git`.
1. Go to your Hostinger hPanel -> **Git** under the website section.
2. Enter the repository URL (`https://github.com/ffcu-FrontField/FrontField.git`) and branch name (`main`).
3. Copy the **Webhook URL** provided by Hostinger.
4. Open your GitHub Repository settings, navigate to **Webhooks** -> **Add Webhook**, paste the Webhook URL, set the Content Type to `application/json`, and save. 
5. Pushing updates to the `main` branch will now automatically deploy the code to your server.

### Option B: Deploy from a New GitHub Repository
If you want to migrate to a new repository:
1. Create a new repository on GitHub (e.g. `https://github.com/username/new-repo.git`).
2. Update the remote URL in your local project terminal:
   ```bash
   git remote set-url origin https://github.com/username/new-repo.git
   ```
3. Push your current codebase to the new repository:
   ```bash
   git push -u origin main
   ```
4. Set up the Git details in Hostinger hPanel using your new repository URL.

